From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Lucas Goossen <lucas.goossen@hey.com>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 17:28:27 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] drm: apple: answer eDP for the J313 backlight and cap
 it at 394 nits

Firmware older than 26 answers create_backlight_service with
dcp_has_panel() only. That stays false until the panel dimensions have
been parsed, which is after 13.5 firmware asks during start_ios_gated.
The firmware then reports that it could not find the Backlight service,
and later backlight writes are ignored until a modeset power cycle.
connector_type is already eDP when the panel node has been read. Answer
an eDP connector on that path the same way firmware 26 and newer does.
External displays are not eDP and still answer false.

J313 BrightnessLCD rejects 395 nits and above: iDAC 1956 is accepted
and 1957 is not. apple,max-brightness is 420, so 100% asks for a level
the firmware drops. Cap apple,panel-j313, and a panel id of J313, at
394 nits. Other panels keep the device-tree maximum, and 100% on this
panel lands on 394.

Measured on a MacBook Air (M1, 2020, J313, DCP firmware 13.5) running
linux-aurora 7.2.11. This commit has not been booted as a new kernel.

Signed-off-by: Lucas Goossen <lucas.goossen@hey.com>
(cherry picked from commit 6f96bfb2f9ab54e7cb42f000713bba2ccc32cb96)
[j604: k610 drm sync: re-applied on Aurora 50d5865ea6 drm/apple. The panel
 is matched by its first compatible only (dcp_panel_is_j313(compatible)):
 the dcp_panel.id fallback came with the J516C EDID wiring, which the sync
 drops (see the previous commit). The create_backlight_service answer is
 made unconditional over upstream's "#if DCP_FW_H17(DCP_FW_VER)" (was
 ">= 26.0.0" here), as the original commit did.]
(cherry picked from commit 84b6574240ce85ae3cf9d2c5120c5b75a93eed59)
(cherry picked from commit b57e0cfe45ce45eae27c487846a8fbeea7c977f5)
Signed-off-by: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/apple/dcp.c            | 30 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 drivers/gpu/drm/apple/iomfb_template.c | 15 ++++++-------
 2 files changed, 37 insertions(+), 8 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/apple/dcp.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/apple/dcp.c
index 61bef7cdc5..f3765d6741 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/apple/dcp.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/apple/dcp.c
@@ -5657,6 +5657,18 @@ static int dcp_ext_wait_pmp(struct apple_dcp *dcp)
 	return 0;
 }
 
+/*
+ * J313 BrightnessLCD::nitsToDBV rejects 395 nits and above.  iDAC 1956 is
+ * accepted and 1957 is not, so 394 is the brightest level that applies.
+ * apple,max-brightness on this panel is 420; 100% must land on 394.
+ */
+#define DCP_J313_MAX_NITS 394U
+
+static bool dcp_panel_is_j313(const char *compatible)
+{
+	return compatible && !strcmp(compatible, "apple,panel-j313");
+}
+
 static int dcp_comp_bind_pipe(struct device *dev, struct device *main, void *data)
 {
 	struct device_node *panel_np;
@@ -5765,6 +5777,8 @@ static int dcp_comp_bind_pipe(struct device *dev, struct device *main, void *dat
 		panel_np = of_get_compatible_child(dev->of_node, "apple,panel");
 
 	if (panel_np) {
+		const char *compatible = NULL;
+
 		if (dcp->fw_compat == DCP_FIRMWARE_V_26_6_DESKTOP) {
 			/*
 			 * Desktop 26.x swaps carry nits, and the panel node
@@ -5783,6 +5797,22 @@ static int dcp_comp_bind_pipe(struct device *dev, struct device *main, void *dat
 		}
 
 		dcp_panel_read_dimensions(dcp, panel_np);
+		if (of_property_read_string_index(panel_np, "compatible", 0,
+						  &compatible))
+			compatible = NULL;
+		/*
+		 * Only this panel.  The backlight device's maximum is this
+		 * value, so 100% asks the firmware for DCP_J313_MAX_NITS.
+		 */
+		if (dcp_panel_is_j313(compatible) &&
+		    dcp->brightness.maximum > DCP_J313_MAX_NITS) {
+			dcp->brightness.maximum = DCP_J313_MAX_NITS;
+			if (dcp->brightness.nits > (int)DCP_J313_MAX_NITS)
+				dcp->brightness.nits = DCP_J313_MAX_NITS;
+			dev_info(dev, "capping panel backlight at %u nits\n",
+				 DCP_J313_MAX_NITS);
+		}
+
 		of_node_put(panel_np);
 		/* Read target metadata for H17P and desktop firmware alike. */
 		dcp_panel_read_adt(dcp);
diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/apple/iomfb_template.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/apple/iomfb_template.c
index bd7927a412..d51a535f38 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/apple/iomfb_template.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/apple/iomfb_template.c
@@ -3210,19 +3210,18 @@ static u32 dcpep_cb_set_tiling_state_v26_6(struct apple_dcp *dcp,
 
 static u8 dcpep_cb_create_backlight_service(struct apple_dcp *dcp)
 {
-#if DCP_FW_H17(DCP_FW_VER)
 	/*
-	 * H17P asks during start_ios_gated, before any mode is known, but
+	 * Firmware asks during start_ios_gated, before any mode is known, but
 	 * dcp_has_panel() only becomes true once the panel dimensions have been
-	 * parsed.  An internal panel always has a backlight, so answer for the
-	 * connector; answering false makes the firmware report that it could
-	 * not find the backlight service.
+	 * parsed.  13.5 does this as well as firmware 26 and newer.  An
+	 * internal panel always has a backlight, so answer for the connector;
+	 * answering false makes the firmware report that it could not find the
+	 * backlight service, and later writes are ignored until a modeset
+	 * power cycle.  connector_type is already eDP when the panel node has
+	 * been read.  External displays are not eDP.
 	 */
 	return dcp_has_panel(dcp) ||
 	       dcp->connector_type == DRM_MODE_CONNECTOR_eDP;
-#else
-	return dcp_has_panel(dcp);
-#endif
 }
 
 TRAMPOLINE_VOID(trampoline_nop, dcpep_cb_nop);
-- 
2.43.0

